  "nonlinear_category": "RETROGRADE",
  "nonlinear_category_reason": "Scene order runs from the latest stretch to the earliest throughout, with no present-day level the telling returns to. The film is assembled and played backwards outright, so an execution reads as a birth and a dismemberment as a woman being put together.",
  "syuzhet_notes": "Every shot is printed and run in reverse, and a narrator reads the result as though it were the right way round, so the film opens on the execution and calls it a birth. The first told bullet is the last thing in the story and the last bullet the first.",
  "fabula_notes": "The bullets record the events in the order a clock would put them, not in the order the reversed narration claims for them.",
